<% content_for :title, "About" %>
<%= render "shared/page_hero", eyebrow: "About", title: "A second view of the technology, taken independently of the people selling it." %>
<div class="page"><div class="wrap split">
  <div class="prose-col">
    <p>I started writing software at thirteen, and I have been building and running technology for 43 years. I have done technical due diligence since 2000. For more than a decade I worked at In-Q-Tel, the venture firm that finds technology for the intelligence community, where much of the work was matching a company to a customer who needed it.</p>
    <p>I started attending family office events in 2018, and that is where I learned how these offices decide: a principal, a family, sometimes a shared team, and a technical question nobody in the room can answer. Parallex exists for that question.</p>
    <p>Parallex has been a company since 2009. I left In-Q-Tel on the last day of 2016, and I could not consult through Parallex while I was there or during the year of contract work that followed. So it stayed small: three investments between 2010 and about 2013, and a few small projects. Each of those investments was cleared with In-Q-Tel's general counsel before I made it. Now it is where I do this work. My wife and I own Parallex. Most engagements are done by a team built for the problem in front of us, and we bring in experts as the work requires. You do not get a standing bench. You get the people your deal needs.</p>

    <h2>The name</h2>
    <p><em>Parallax</em> is looking at one thing from two angles. The offset between the views tells you its depth. That is the job: a second view of a company's technology, taken independently of the people selling it.</p>

    <p><%= link_to "Request an introduction", new_introduction_path, class: "btn" %></p>
  </div>

